# The MINIMAL pinned base every artifact starts from. Add this path's own
# dependencies below, one per line, each pinned with `==`.
#
# COMPILE IT, NEVER HAND-EDIT requirements.txt:
#
#     uv pip compile requirements.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#         -o requirements.txt
#
# THE `--generate-hashes` FLAG IS NOT OPTIONAL. Install with
# `--require-hashes`, which refuses the ENTIRE install if a single hash is
# missing. Transitive pins are the part a human gets wrong, and a lock whose
# hashes are partly hand-maintained fails open on exactly the package nobody
# checked.
#
# NO RANGE SPECIFIER OF ANY KIND, HERE OR IN THE COMPILED OUTPUT. Not `>=`, not
# `,<`, not `~=`, not `!=`. This is a real committed defect elsewhere, not a
# hypothetical: a shipped artifact in this program carries `elasticsearch>=8,<9`
# in its requirements, which is why that file is now a known-bad fixture rather
# than a model. A range means two people running the same command on different
# days measure different software and report it as the same benchmark.
#
# The artifact run chain itself -- gate, derive, render, verify, provenance,
# finalize, and the vendored core -- is deliberately dependency-free standard
# library, so it keeps working after any resolution here. pytest is the only
# base requirement.
pytest==9.1.1
